🗄️ DATABASE CONNECTIVITY (JDBC) – ORAL CHEAT SHEET
⭐ 1. JDBC (INTRODUCTION)
JDBC (Java Database Connectivity) is an API used to connect Java programs with databases like MySQL or PostgreSQL.
👉 It allows:
Connecting to database
Executing SQL queries
Fetching results
⭐ 2. JDBC ARCHITECTURE
Steps:
Java Application
JDBC API
Driver Manager
JDBC Driver
Database
⭐ 3. JDBC STEPS (VERY IMPORTANT FOR VIVA)
✔ Step 1: Load Driver
Java
Class.forName("com.mysql.cj.jdbc.Driver");
✔ Step 2: Create Connection
Java
Connection con = DriverManager.getConnection(
"jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/test", "root", "password");
✔ Step 3: Create Statement
Java
Statement stmt = con.createStatement();
✔ Step 4: Execute Query
Java
ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery("SELECT * FROM student");
✔ Step 5: Close Connection
Java
con.close();
⭐ 4. CONNECTING JAVA WITH MYSQL / POSTGRESQL
MySQL URL:

jdbc:mysql://localhost:3306/dbname
PostgreSQL URL:

jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/dbname
⭐ 5. CRUD OPERATIONS USING JDBC
CRUD = Create, Read, Update, Delete
✔ INSERT
Java
stmt.executeUpdate("INSERT INTO student VALUES (1,'Riya')");
✔ SELECT
Java
ResultSet rs = stmt.executeQuery("SELECT * FROM student");
✔ UPDATE
Java
stmt.executeUpdate("UPDATE student SET name='Anu' WHERE id=1");
✔ DELETE
Java
stmt.executeUpdate("DELETE FROM student WHERE id=1");
⭐ 6. PREPARED STATEMENT
Used to prevent SQL injection and improve performance.
Java
PreparedStatement ps = con.prepareStatement(
"INSERT INTO student VALUES (?, ?)");

ps.setInt(1, 1);
ps.setString(2, "Riya");
ps.executeUpdate();
👉 Advantages:
Secure
Faster for repeated queries
🧾 ONE-LINE JDBC ANSWERS
✔ JDBC: API to connect Java with database
✔ Connection: Link between Java and DB
✔ Statement: Used to execute SQL queries
✔ ResultSet: Stores query result
✔ PreparedStatement: Precompiled SQL statement
✔ CRUD: Create, Read, Update, Delete
⚡ JDBC TRICK QUESTIONS
Q1. Why JDBC is used?
To connect Java applications with databases.
Q2. Difference between Statement and PreparedStatement?
PreparedStatement is faster and secure.
Q3. What is ResultSet?
Object that stores data retrieved from database.
Q4. Why Class.forName()?
To load JDBC driver.
